c meow of all time  sky hook extraction the dark knight  next up we have the sky hook extraction  scene from 2008's the dark knight who is  batman extracting that would be mr wow a  chinese crime lord and accountant who is  also the ceo of lao security investments  with gotham's major crimes unit cracking  down on money laundering services  throughout the city allow fleas to an  undisclosed location to protect the  mafia's money but with all apologies to  joker's question let's be serious you  can't hide from bail man and soon lau's  precise location is discovered he's held  up in a skyscraper in hong kong with an  army of paid guards ready to protect him  by any means necessary obviously batman  isn't swayed by the less than ideal  circumstances and since his memory cloth  cape isn't built for long distance  flights like you know gotham to hong  kong he's got a ride in a cargo plane  used by hired smugglers as batman  infiltrates laos building from above  he's swarmed by guards but fights them  off and successfully grabs hold of wow  dragging him toward a large window and  then using him as a human shield against  the encroaching police force his back is  literally against the wall but timed  explosives blast the building windows  open and batman and lao fly out pulled  up by a small balloon that then latches  onto the cargo plane that is perfectly  positioned overhead  it's a flawlessly executed extraction  and batman successfully brings lao back  to gotham to face justice not that all  superhero movies are required to explain  themselves when something seems too  far-fetched to believe that's kind of  the point of the word super but this  sequence definitely left more than a few  people saying yeah right nolan that  would never work and they'd be wrong  because this scene was directly based on  a real cia program called sky hook also  known as the fulton surface-to-air  recovery system the program was designed  to help rescue downed pilots or fleeing  spies who were stranded behind enemy  lines the downed pilot would deploy a  small balloon strap themselves in and  wait for a passing aircraft to grab the  line and pull them up and out of harm's  way we all stand corrected mr nolan  batman v superman batman v superman dawn  of  men are justice  you can't call your movie batman be  superman and not have a scene where  batman fights superman luckily zack  snyder understood this and gave us  exactly what we wanted to see and  additionally aim to solve the ancient  debate of who would win in a fight  between the man of steel and the caped  crusader unfortunately the clear winner  isn't so easy to determine though  strictly on a physical level it appears  that batman ends up having the upper  hand and superman is at his mercy but  it's important to understand the context  of this fight and the events leading up  to this legendary scene first of all  superman does not want to fight batman  he makes that explicitly clear from the  start of this encounter though batman  refuses to listen and is hell bent on  confrontation superman wants batman's  help in fighting and saving his mother  and feels that their combined powers can  bring down supervillain lex luthor  kent begs fat man to come to his senses  pleading bruce please i was wrong you  have to listen to me but batman  unleashes his fury even after several  violent exchanges kent tries to keep the  peace sadly batman crosses the point of  no return when he sneakily expends a  large dose of kryptonian gas crippling  superman and leaving him unable to  defend himself which batman takes full  advantage of as the sequence plays out  we're left wondering why is batman so  angry with superman and beyond reason  it's because superman destroyed  metropolis and batman was present to see  this destruction firsthand right or  maybe it's because batman feels  threatened by superman's alien powers  and sees him as a threat to the safety  of the entire planet or is like sleuther  masterminding their rivalry and pitting  the two against each other or maybe it's  just a simple case of caitlyn  saving the swat team and hostages the  dark knight  doctors get down live  the next scene was designed to be one of  the boats the best of all time there's a  countdown thugs hostages explosives the  swat team and of course clowns  lots and lots of clowns the bulk of this  scene takes place in the pruitt building  where the jokers placed a bunch of  hostages and disguised them as armed  thugs in clown masks as the swat team  moves in batman has already taken  matters into his own hands attacking who  he thinks are the joker's thugs after  subduing one of these thug clowns and  ripping off their mask he informs fox  that the swats are targeting the wrong  people and that the clowns are actually  the hostages and i love that i just got  to say that sentence  we got him he's out of the game  [Music]  commissioner gordon is preoccupied with  a distressing phone call courtesy of two  faced and the swats are already in  motion with snipers on the adjacent  rooftop and their entry team quickly  climbing the stairs in that moment  batman has no choice but to fight the  swat team to keep them from killing the  hostages they believe to be the  criminals it's complete chaos and once  again batman appears to be the bad guy  when in reality we know he's the hero  the joker's ruse is eventually uncovered  and batman does end up saving hostages  and keeping the swat team mostly safe  but not before some serious edge of your  seat action and some likely hospital  bills batman interrogates joker the dark  knight you've changed things  forever then why do you want to kill me  i don't want to kill you  what would i do without you go back to  ripping off mob dealers no no  no  no you you complete  me you're garbage you kills for money  don't talk like one of them you're not  even if you'd like to be  last up we have the scene where batman  interrogates joker in nolan's the dark  knight this film is considered to be one  of the greatest if not the single  greatest batman ever made christian bale  is brilliant as always and michael kane  gary oldman aaron eckhart maggie  gyllenhaal and morgan freeman are all  top shelf but what really set this film  apart was heath ledger's portrayal of  the joker just stepping into that role  in the first place would have been  difficult knowing that nicholson had  already set the bar so high the ledger  not only accepted the lofty position he  also completely reinterpreted the  character and added a layer of depth  never before reached by any super  villain the true brilliance of ledger's  joker can be witnessed during the  interrogation scene where batman  impatiently demands to know where dent  and rachel are being held the joker gets  inside batman's head playing  psychological tricks and frustrating him  to the point that he becomes agitated  and violent  where are we  killing is making a choice  where are they choose between one line  for the other your friendly district  attorney or his brushing bride-to-be  you have nothing  nothing to threaten me  one line of jokers is especially  poignant when he says to them you're  just a freak like me they need you right  now when they don't they'll cast you out  these words cut like a knife and you can  feel batman's anger shift to emotional  pain in this moment but he snaps out of  it and lifts joker up by his shirt once  again demanding answers the joker  doesn't let up and though batman  continues beating him he just laughs  harder and talks more almost  re-energized by the pain according to  bale this was their first scene shot  together and he saw that heath ledger  was quote a hell of an actor who's  completely committed and totally gets  the tone that nolan is trying to create  bale added that ledger demanded to be  hit for real and was egging him on  during takes ledger's portrayal of joker  won him a posthumous oscar for best  supporting actor and goes down in  history as one of the most haunting and  remarkable performances ever regardless  of genre and there you have it our picks  for the best batman scenes of all time  as always we couldn't cover every iconic  batman scene to ever hit the big screen  but there's plenty more episodes of rt  essentials on the way so fear not i'm  sure we'll get there eventually thanks  for tuning in i'm mark ellis and  remember  you  complete me  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

